titre$ Cyphellaceae Cooke 1961
com$ adampt GF avril 2017
1,0$ source : W . Bridge Cooke -1961- The Cyphellaceous Fungi A Study in the Porotheleaceae/// Beihefte Zur Sydowia, Numéro 4
1,0$

1,0 $ Spores angular $ Rhodocyphella
1,2 $ Spores smooth
2,3 $ Receptacles fasciculate or conglobate
2,4 $ Receptacles separate, rarely occurring so close together as to appear fasciculate or conglobate, or rarely with branched stipes
3,0 $ Receptacles fasciculate $ Merismodes
3,0 $ Receptacles conglobate $ Stromatoscyphella
4,0 $ Receptacles covered with brown hairs, of which at least some have inflated tips $ Cyphellopsis
4,5 $ Receptacles without such surface hairs
5,6 $ Receptacles without special surface hairs, or if these are present they are mycelioid or without incrusting granules
5,8 $ Receptacles with special granule-incrusted surface hairs, hairs usually with thick walls
6,0 $ Receptacles without special surface hairs or with mycelioid surface, usually stipitate, campanulate $ Calyptella
6,7 $ Receptacles cupulate, with or without special hairs
7,0 $ Receptacles without special surface hairs $ Glabrocyphella
7,0 $ Receptacles with smooth surface hairs $ Cellypha
8,9 $ Surface hairs hyaline to pale colored
8,0 $ Surface hairs yellow to brown $ Maireina
9,10 $ Receptacles cupulate
9,11 $ Receptacles cylindric
10,0 $ Granules formed of minute crystalline material $ Lachnella
10,0 $ Granules formed of large acicular crystals $ Flagelloscypha
11,0 $ Spores globose or ovate $ Solenia
11,0 $ Spores fusiform $ Woldmaria
